        "original_id": "78ece239-1534-5ab0-962a-95db01b8444e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hans Schlegel, Frank De Winne, Dirk Frimout\n- Organizations: ESA, NASA, ISS Expedition 21, Belgian Air Component\n- Roles: Physicist, astronaut, officer, commander\n\nFacts:\n- Hans Schlegel was born in Überlingen on 3 August 1951.\n- Hans Schlegel is a German physicist, an ESA astronaut, and a veteran of two NASA Space Shuttle missions.\n- Frank De Winne was born in Ledeberg, Belgium, on 25 April 1961.\n- Frank De Winne is a Belgian Air Component officer and an ESA astronaut.\n- Frank De Winne became Belgium's second person in space after Dirk Frimout.\n- Frank De Winne was the first ESA astronaut to command a space mission when he served as commander of ISS Expedition 21.",
